       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 20 mg is twice the FDA-labeled maximum of 10 mg once daily for adults. Doses above 10 mg raise the risk of peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia, and they usually add little blood pressure benefit.\n\nWhich of these do you want?\n\n1. **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily**, the maximum standard dose.\n2. **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily**, if this is a starting dose.\n3. **Amlodipine 20 mg PO once daily as written**, if the dose is intentional. If so, please confirm and I'll enter it with a note recording that it is above the usual maximum.\n\nIf the goal is more blood pressure control, adding a second agent such as an ARB, an ACE inhibitor, or a thiazide is usually preferred to going above 10 mg. Tell me which option you want and I'll enter it."
      }
